  Slack / Firefox / ClickUp / alertd ...
          │  Notify() call on the D-Bus session bus
          ▼
  ┌──────────────────┐
  │  dbus-monitor    │  child process, prints each call as text
  └────────┬─────────┘
           │ stdout pipe (line by line)
  ┌────────▼──────────────────── python app.py (one process) ──────────────┐
  │                                                                        │
  │  [listener thread]  listen_dbus()                                      │
  │     parse text → app_name, summary, body                               │
  │     resolve empty app_name via .desktop files (snap.slack → "Slack")   │
  │     save_notification(): drop duplicates seen within 2s                │
  │          │                         │                                   │
  │          ▼                         ▼                                   │
  │   INSERT into SQLite        broadcast() → one queue per open tab       │
  │   notifications.db                 │                                   │
  │          ▲                         │                                   │
  │  [Flask/Werkzeug server, one thread per request]                       │
  │     GET  /notifications ──── read all rows                             │
  │     PATCH .../check, .../comment ── update a row                       │
  │     GET  /stream ─────────── waits on its queue, sends each new item   │
  │     /wallpaper ──────────── wallpaper.* file in the app folder         │
  │     /server/restart|stop ── exit 42 / exit 0                           │
  └──────────────────────────────┬─────────────────────────────────────────┘
                                 │ HTTP on 0.0.0.0:5000
                       ┌─────────▼──────────┐
                       │ Browser page       │  index.html, plain JavaScript
                       │ loads list, then   │  filter, sort, appearance
                       │ live via /stream   │  saved in localStorage
                       └────────────────────┘
  systemd user service: keeps the process running and restarts it on failure
